1
00:01:42,660 --> 00:01:48,000
[When I Meet The Moon]

2
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:50,950
[Episode 2]

3
00:01:58,289 --> 00:01:59,289
Ms. Idle Cloud,

4
00:01:59,430 --> 00:02:00,430
you're so early.

5
00:02:00,780 --> 00:02:01,780
Take a seat first.

6
00:02:03,070 --> 00:02:04,070
Jiameng.

7
00:02:04,390 --> 00:02:05,720
Have a seat. Here.

8
00:02:05,870 --> 00:02:06,870
Okay.

9
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:13,560
Everyone, take a seat first.

10
00:02:14,060 --> 00:02:14,710
Let me tell you,

11
00:02:14,711 --> 00:02:15,809
I'll ask for your help again

12
00:02:15,810 --> 00:02:16,680
for the next test.

13
00:02:16,681 --> 00:02:17,750
Sure, no problem.

14
00:02:23,090 --> 00:02:24,090
Ms. Idle Cloud,

15
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:26,060
are you looking for someone?

16
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:28,000
N-No.

17
00:02:50,470 --> 00:02:51,730
How did you end up here?

18
00:02:53,130 --> 00:02:54,130
Come, sit here.

19
00:02:58,130 --> 00:02:59,990
I thought you didn't like crowds.

20
00:03:01,860 --> 00:03:02,860
I'm hungry.

21
00:03:04,910 --> 00:03:06,640
The view here is not bad, right?

22
00:03:08,060 --> 00:03:10,060
When Mr. Xu and Shize sit together,

23
00:03:10,120 --> 00:03:13,050
it's a total paradise for
people who love good looks.

24
00:03:17,870 --> 00:03:19,809
What does Shize do

25
00:03:19,810 --> 00:03:21,280
at EAW?

26
00:03:21,810 --> 00:03:23,180
He's a friend of Mr. Xu

27
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:25,540
who came over to help before the opening.

28
00:03:26,020 --> 00:03:27,620
He is very handsome,

29
00:03:27,810 --> 00:03:29,060
but he's too cold.

30
00:03:29,190 --> 00:03:30,920
I don't even dare to talk to him.

31
00:03:40,190 --> 00:03:41,370
Hello, everyone!

32
00:03:41,690 --> 00:03:42,750
Everyone's here?

33
00:03:44,260 --> 00:03:45,440
Who is this?

34
00:03:45,470 --> 00:03:47,190
Ms. Feifei,
you're dressed so extravagantly.

35
00:03:47,290 --> 00:03:48,559
You're stealing the show!

36
00:03:48,560 --> 00:03:50,090
Mr. K, don't talk nonsense.

37
00:03:50,470 --> 00:03:51,470
Take a seat.

38
00:03:52,900 --> 00:03:53,900
Handsome,

39
00:03:53,960 --> 00:03:55,179
this seat is empty.

40
00:03:55,180 --> 00:03:56,620
Do you mind if I sit here?

41
00:03:56,960 --> 00:03:57,960
I do.

42
00:03:59,670 --> 00:04:01,130
It's fine. Just sit there.

43
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:10,520
Handsome,

44
00:04:10,870 --> 00:04:12,459
are you Mr. Xu's friend?

45
00:04:12,460 --> 00:04:13,469
You flew the drone

46
00:04:13,470 --> 00:04:14,960
so well today.

47
00:04:15,650 --> 00:04:17,579
Can you teach me when you have time?

48
00:04:21,100 --> 00:04:22,510
This social butterfly.

49
00:04:22,690 --> 00:04:23,889
She went after Mr. Xu during the day,

50
00:04:23,890 --> 00:04:25,859
and now she's targeting someone else.

51
00:04:25,860 --> 00:04:27,389
I realized I haven't introduced myself yet.

52
00:04:27,390 --> 00:04:28,750
I'm Fairy Feifei.

53
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:30,220
Just call me Feifei.

54
00:04:42,180 --> 00:04:44,010
Cheers! Come on, cheers.

55
00:05:27,890 --> 00:05:29,020
You want to eat this?

56
00:05:29,430 --> 00:05:30,560
Let me get it for you.

57
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:32,040
No need.

58
00:05:35,600 --> 00:05:37,430
Was he turning the table for me?

59
00:05:49,060 --> 00:05:49,620
Come!

60
00:05:49,621 --> 00:05:50,880
Let me propose a toast.

61
00:05:50,920 --> 00:05:52,720
Everyone has worked hard today.

62
00:05:52,980 --> 00:05:54,809
Thank you, Mr. Xu.

63
00:05:54,810 --> 00:05:55,830
Good job.

64
00:06:00,830 --> 00:06:02,310
I wonder if anyone
has any suggestions

65
00:06:02,430 --> 00:06:03,630
for EAW?

66
00:06:03,920 --> 00:06:05,479
Before the official opening,

67
00:06:05,480 --> 00:06:06,420
is there anything

68
00:06:06,421 --> 00:06:07,820
that needs improvement?

69
00:06:08,030 --> 00:06:10,310
Please speak freely.

70
00:06:10,630 --> 00:06:12,420
There's nothing to improve.

71
00:06:12,540 --> 00:06:13,810
It's already the best.

72
00:06:14,630 --> 00:06:16,680
Only EAW could reach

73
00:06:16,720 --> 00:06:17,130
such high standards

74
00:06:17,131 --> 00:06:18,570
within the country.

75
00:06:19,130 --> 00:06:20,329
How else to improve, isn't it?

76
00:06:20,330 --> 00:06:21,510
Mr. K is right.

77
00:06:21,580 --> 00:06:23,100
EAW is the best.

78
00:06:23,240 --> 00:06:23,980
We really

79
00:06:23,981 --> 00:06:25,910
broadened our horizons this time.

80
00:06:25,920 --> 00:06:27,070
Ms. Idle Cloud,

81
00:06:27,810 --> 00:06:29,870
why haven't you talked much tonight?

82
00:06:30,190 --> 00:06:31,190
Feifei.

83
00:06:31,770 --> 00:06:33,100
Ms. Idle Cloud

84
00:06:33,130 --> 00:06:34,770
is very introverted,

85
00:06:35,310 --> 00:06:37,310
so stop making it difficult for her.

86
00:06:37,540 --> 00:06:38,919
How are you a content creator

87
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:40,309
when you are this introverted?

88
00:06:40,310 --> 00:06:41,440
Just say a few words.

89
00:06:41,620 --> 00:06:42,869
We're not going to eat you,

90
00:06:42,870 --> 00:06:43,870
right?
Yeah, yeah.

91
00:06:44,310 --> 00:06:45,310
That's right.

92
00:06:48,190 --> 00:06:50,070
It's clearly a normal word.

93
00:06:50,570 --> 00:06:51,720
How did it become

94
00:06:51,750 --> 00:06:53,250
a derogatory term?

95
00:06:53,640 --> 00:06:54,840
Ms. Idle Cloud,

96
00:06:55,050 --> 00:06:57,450
it is indeed not good
to be too introverted.

97
00:06:57,940 --> 00:06:58,800
I feel that

98
00:06:58,830 --> 00:07:01,560
introversion is just a personal trait,

99
00:07:01,920 --> 00:07:03,040
not a flaw.

100
00:07:04,260 --> 00:07:05,260
This...

101
00:07:05,310 --> 00:07:06,870
Ms. Idle Cloud Tick-Tock

102
00:07:07,310 --> 00:07:08,430
thought for so long

103
00:07:08,510 --> 00:07:10,240
just to say this one sentence?

104
00:07:13,810 --> 00:07:16,140
Introverted people are good at thinking.

105
00:07:17,630 --> 00:07:18,829
At least they don't talk nonsense

106
00:07:18,830 --> 00:07:19,920
without thinking.

107
00:07:25,220 --> 00:07:26,220
Well,

108
00:07:26,810 --> 00:07:29,410
that can't be considered
an advantage, right?

109
00:07:42,070 --> 00:07:43,230
It's still early.
Why don't we

110
00:07:43,540 --> 00:07:44,810
play a game together?

111
00:07:45,010 --> 00:07:47,200
Why do we still have to play games?

112
00:07:47,220 --> 00:07:48,820
Let's play the simplest one.

113
00:07:48,980 --> 00:07:50,420
Exchanging whispers.

114
00:07:50,770 --> 00:07:52,829
The same phrase is passed down from

115
00:07:52,830 --> 00:07:54,240
the first person in turn,

116
00:07:54,620 --> 00:07:56,009
but you must keep your voice down

117
00:07:56,010 --> 00:07:58,010
so that a third person can't hear it.

118
00:07:59,810 --> 00:08:02,070
Then let's start counterclockwise.

119
00:08:02,730 --> 00:08:03,860
Counterclockwise?

120
00:08:04,310 --> 00:08:05,370
That means

121
00:08:05,620 --> 00:08:07,220
I have to pass it to my left...

122
00:08:11,940 --> 00:08:13,070
Counterclockwise?

123
00:08:13,920 --> 00:08:14,920
Sorry,

124
00:08:15,070 --> 00:08:16,200
can we switch seats?

125
00:08:19,930 --> 00:08:20,920
I am having a cold,

126
00:08:20,921 --> 00:08:22,039
but the air vent is right over there.

127
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:23,300
I'm feeling a bit cold.

128
00:08:23,350 --> 00:08:25,179
He is not yet recovered from his cold?

129
00:08:25,180 --> 00:08:27,140
Why... is he switching seats?

130
00:08:28,540 --> 00:08:29,540
That's fine.
Thank you.

131
00:08:47,530 --> 00:08:48,530
Well...

132
00:08:51,550 --> 00:08:52,550
I...

133
00:08:54,580 --> 00:08:55,719
If I ask him

134
00:08:55,720 --> 00:08:57,520
if he can hear from his right ear,

135
00:08:57,530 --> 00:08:59,060
would it be too deliberate?

136
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:01,460
Never mind. It's nothing.

137
00:09:25,550 --> 00:09:26,550
Come closer.

138
00:09:30,500 --> 00:09:31,500
Move closer.

139
00:10:14,150 --> 00:10:15,219
So when we played

140
00:10:15,220 --> 00:10:16,600
Wings of the Sky today,

141
00:10:17,010 --> 00:10:18,149
he already noticed

142
00:10:18,150 --> 00:10:20,210
that I couldn't hear with my left ear.

143
00:10:45,740 --> 00:10:46,889
That was one

144
00:10:46,890 --> 00:10:48,480
nerve-racking meal.

145
00:11:04,340 --> 00:11:05,030
Hello.

146
00:11:05,031 --> 00:11:06,980
Can I add you on WeChat?

147
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:16,000
What did you say?

148
00:11:16,720 --> 00:11:19,290
I...

149
00:11:21,790 --> 00:11:23,999
Thank you for speaking up for me

150
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:25,200
at the table just now.

151
00:11:28,270 --> 00:11:29,270
You're welcome.

152
00:11:34,790 --> 00:11:35,790
You asked me

153
00:11:36,480 --> 00:11:37,740
to come closer just now

154
00:11:37,840 --> 00:11:39,170
because you knew I...

155
00:11:41,530 --> 00:11:43,330
Why aren't you saying anything?

156
00:11:43,530 --> 00:11:44,590
You didn't finish.

157
00:11:47,510 --> 00:11:48,440
I wanted to ask,

158
00:11:48,441 --> 00:11:49,479
w-why did you

159
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:50,740
tell me to come closer?

160
00:11:54,010 --> 00:11:55,010
The rules.

161
00:11:56,890 --> 00:11:58,820
We can't let a third person hear us.

162
00:12:04,220 --> 00:12:05,220
Shize.

163
00:12:05,720 --> 00:12:06,720
Shall we go?

164
00:12:10,360 --> 00:12:11,760
If there's nothing else,

165
00:12:12,270 --> 00:12:13,470
I'll head over first.

166
00:13:03,980 --> 00:13:04,980
Lili.
How was it?

167
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:06,610
Did it go well today?

168
00:13:07,210 --> 00:13:08,520
It went pretty well.

169
00:13:08,720 --> 00:13:09,720
That's good.

170
00:13:10,010 --> 00:13:11,010
Tangy.

171
00:13:11,220 --> 00:13:12,820
Do you remember

172
00:13:13,340 --> 00:13:15,009
when I was in high school,

173
00:13:15,010 --> 00:13:16,540
I mentioned someone to you?

174
00:13:17,120 --> 00:13:17,910
Who is it?

175
00:13:18,130 --> 00:13:19,030
Aren't you just on average terms

176
00:13:19,031 --> 00:13:20,960
with your high school classmates?

177
00:13:21,220 --> 00:13:22,669
He's not a high school classmate.

178
00:13:22,670 --> 00:13:23,670
He's the one

179
00:13:24,120 --> 00:13:25,140
from XUST.

180
00:13:29,720 --> 00:13:31,579
Is he the one whom you described as

181
00:13:31,580 --> 00:13:32,410
radiant,

182
00:13:32,580 --> 00:13:33,630
full of vitality,

183
00:13:33,670 --> 00:13:34,739
embodying both talent and looks,

184
00:13:34,740 --> 00:13:36,139
and is like a moon in your heart?

185
00:13:36,140 --> 00:13:37,269
You even enshrined his photo

186
00:13:37,270 --> 00:13:38,929
and almost lighted incense for him.

187
00:13:38,930 --> 00:13:39,930
Alright, say no more.

188
00:13:41,820 --> 00:13:43,280
Why bring him up suddenly?

189
00:13:43,820 --> 00:13:46,050
I saw him.

190
00:13:46,440 --> 00:13:47,580
Really?

191
00:13:47,820 --> 00:13:48,820
Where?
In Nanwu?

192
00:13:50,630 --> 00:13:52,269
He's the

193
00:13:52,270 --> 00:13:54,130
Umbrella Killer I told you about.

194
00:13:54,740 --> 00:13:55,840
It's him!

195
00:13:57,270 --> 00:13:58,670
But...

196
00:13:58,740 --> 00:14:00,219
I feel like he's

197
00:14:00,220 --> 00:14:01,750
a bit different now.

198
00:14:03,270 --> 00:14:05,240
But exactly what's different?

199
00:14:05,620 --> 00:14:06,620
I...
Hold on.

200
00:14:07,370 --> 00:14:08,370
Don't say it now.

201
00:14:08,371 --> 00:14:09,599
Wait until I get to Nanwu tomorrow,

202
00:14:09,600 --> 00:14:11,029
then we can have a good chat.

203
00:14:11,030 --> 00:14:12,370
I want to say it now...

204
00:14:15,580 --> 00:14:17,370
You never let me finish.

205
00:14:30,260 --> 00:14:33,140
[Child prodigy skips grades and tops
the college entrance exam in Nanwu]

206
00:14:41,580 --> 00:14:43,220
How is he different?

207
00:14:47,510 --> 00:14:48,510
Forget it.

208
00:14:48,670 --> 00:14:49,670
Go to sleep.

209
00:15:02,550 --> 00:15:04,220
[EAW, Ms. He]

210
00:15:07,410 --> 00:15:08,410
Hello.

211
00:15:08,940 --> 00:15:09,940
Ms. Idle Cloud,

212
00:15:10,010 --> 00:15:11,079
I would like to ask

213
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:12,439
when you are returning

214
00:15:12,440 --> 00:15:14,079
so we can book a ticket for you.

215
00:15:14,080 --> 00:15:15,080
No need to book.

216
00:15:15,081 --> 00:15:17,339
I won't be returning to Xifu anytime soon.

217
00:15:17,340 --> 00:15:19,739
In that case, I'll extend
your stay for another week.

218
00:15:19,740 --> 00:15:20,740
Thank you guys.

219
00:15:21,310 --> 00:15:22,310
Thanks.

220
00:15:32,870 --> 00:15:35,530
That saves me a week's rent.

221
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:39,080
That's great.

222
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:01,960
You brat!

223
00:16:02,080 --> 00:16:03,219
Don't you have eyes?

224
00:16:03,220 --> 00:16:04,556
This is a sidewalk.
Can't you see it?

225
00:16:04,580 --> 00:16:05,410
You were driving so fast!

226
00:16:05,411 --> 00:16:06,940
Who's the one without eyes?

227
00:16:07,900 --> 00:16:09,850
What? "Driving"?

228
00:16:09,880 --> 00:16:11,080
This isn't even a car!

229
00:16:11,120 --> 00:16:13,180
How is it not a car when it has 4 wheels?

230
00:16:14,620 --> 00:16:15,680
You call this a car?

231
00:16:17,080 --> 00:16:17,720
Old Auntie.

232
00:16:17,721 --> 00:16:19,980
I really don't have time to mess with you.

233
00:16:21,980 --> 00:16:22,980
Old Auntie?

234
00:16:23,500 --> 00:16:25,160
Who are you calling an auntie?

235
00:16:25,940 --> 00:16:27,400
Is there anyone else here?

236
00:16:30,720 --> 00:16:31,320
Old Auntie,

237
00:16:31,321 --> 00:16:32,369
maybe you're getting old

238
00:16:32,370 --> 00:16:33,769
and your aim is getting worse.

239
00:16:33,770 --> 00:16:35,129
Remember to throw more
accurately the next time.

240
00:16:35,130 --> 00:16:36,130
Bye!

241
00:16:36,630 --> 00:16:38,360
Don't let me run into you again!

242
00:16:39,520 --> 00:16:41,040
I am so scared, Old Auntie.

243
00:17:09,089 --> 00:17:10,089
Tangy!
Lili!

244
00:17:11,200 --> 00:17:12,700
I missed you so much.

245
00:17:13,270 --> 00:17:14,109
It's been so long,

246
00:17:14,110 --> 00:17:15,439
and we finally meet again.

247
00:17:15,440 --> 00:17:16,608
You brought something?

248
00:17:16,609 --> 00:17:18,179
I brought you some fresh peaches.

249
00:17:18,180 --> 00:17:18,680
Really?

250
00:17:18,681 --> 00:17:20,510
I was just craving some fruit.

251
00:17:20,740 --> 00:17:22,470
Thanks for the food, my friend.

252
00:17:25,400 --> 00:17:26,180
But my friend,

253
00:17:26,181 --> 00:17:27,940
these are fresh peaches?

254
00:17:29,570 --> 00:17:31,230
Speaking of this makes me mad.

255
00:17:31,400 --> 00:17:33,130
I just ran into this brat

256
00:17:33,330 --> 00:17:34,509
riding his stupid skateboard,

257
00:17:34,510 --> 00:17:36,286
bumping into things left and right.
He knocked all my peaches

258
00:17:36,310 --> 00:17:37,329
to the ground.

259
00:17:37,330 --> 00:17:38,809
It took me forever to pick them up.

260
00:17:38,810 --> 00:17:39,460
It's okay.

261
00:17:39,740 --> 00:17:41,269
At least they're still edible.

262
00:17:41,270 --> 00:17:42,439
I told him off

263
00:17:42,440 --> 00:17:43,639
and he got mad instead.

264
00:17:43,640 --> 00:17:45,069
Do you know what he called me?

265
00:17:45,070 --> 00:17:45,740
What?

266
00:17:45,741 --> 00:17:46,880
Old Auntie.

267
00:17:49,640 --> 00:17:51,069
I'm in my prime

268
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:53,070
and shining with my natural beauty.

269
00:17:53,420 --> 00:17:55,239
Which eye of his saw that I was old?

270
00:17:55,240 --> 00:17:56,329
Don't lower yourself

271
00:17:56,330 --> 00:17:56,830
to that brat's level.

272
00:17:56,831 --> 00:17:58,659
Our Tangy is the most
beautiful in the world.

273
00:17:58,660 --> 00:17:59,990
Number one in the world.

274
00:18:00,940 --> 00:18:01,640
Let's not talk about him.

275
00:18:01,641 --> 00:18:02,770
What bad luck.

276
00:18:03,770 --> 00:18:04,810
Have you had breakfast?
No.

277
00:18:05,880 --> 00:18:06,880
Let's go.

278
00:18:06,920 --> 00:18:07,810
And tell me more about

279
00:18:07,811 --> 00:18:09,330
your first love.

280
00:18:13,440 --> 00:18:15,029
I remember it was almost the senior year,

281
00:18:15,030 --> 00:18:17,179
yet you would still go to XUST every day.

282
00:18:17,180 --> 00:18:18,000
I originally thought

283
00:18:18,001 --> 00:18:20,089
you'd neglect your
studies for a handsome guy.

284
00:18:20,090 --> 00:18:20,530
I didn't expect you

285
00:18:20,531 --> 00:18:22,030
to make him your goal,

286
00:18:22,380 --> 00:18:24,000
and you worked so hard then.

287
00:18:25,550 --> 00:18:27,179
The day you failed the exam,

288
00:18:27,180 --> 00:18:28,510
you cried your eyes out.

289
00:18:28,830 --> 00:18:29,200
After that,

290
00:18:29,201 --> 00:18:30,829
I never heard you mention him again.

291
00:18:30,830 --> 00:18:32,499
It's really meant to be

292
00:18:32,500 --> 00:18:34,360
if you could meet again like this.

293
00:18:35,740 --> 00:18:36,740
I didn't expect

294
00:18:37,380 --> 00:18:38,769
to meet him again either,

295
00:18:38,770 --> 00:18:41,180
and of all places, in Nanwu.

296
00:18:43,330 --> 00:18:44,240
Shouldn't he be

297
00:18:44,241 --> 00:18:45,589
doing his Ph.D. at XUST now?

298
00:18:45,590 --> 00:18:46,590
Why is he at EAW?

299
00:18:47,900 --> 00:18:48,999
If we calculate the time,

300
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:50,930
he probably hasn't graduated yet.

301
00:18:51,500 --> 00:18:53,380
I'm wondering about this too.

302
00:18:54,700 --> 00:18:55,939
We don't need to dwell on it.

303
00:18:55,940 --> 00:18:57,940
Why don't you just ask him directly?

304
00:19:00,160 --> 00:19:01,160
I...

305
00:19:02,740 --> 00:19:03,740
Well...

306
00:19:05,310 --> 00:19:06,710
Did you add him on WeChat?

307
00:19:08,830 --> 00:19:09,440
No.

308
00:19:09,740 --> 00:19:10,879
Don't tell me you don't even have

309
00:19:10,880 --> 00:19:12,770
the courage to ask for his WeChat.

310
00:19:15,250 --> 00:19:16,250
Just eat.

311
00:19:24,830 --> 00:19:25,830
Lili,

312
00:19:26,180 --> 00:19:27,479
do you plan to let it all go

313
00:19:27,480 --> 00:19:28,829
without a trace,

314
00:19:28,830 --> 00:19:30,069
and let it drift away

315
00:19:30,070 --> 00:19:31,109
like smoke in the wind?

316
00:19:31,110 --> 00:19:32,880
What else can I do?

317
00:19:33,380 --> 00:19:34,830
Then try a little harder.

318
00:19:36,070 --> 00:19:37,070
How?

319
00:19:40,440 --> 00:19:40,850
Find a day

320
00:19:40,851 --> 00:19:42,180
to go wander around EAW.

321
00:19:42,220 --> 00:19:44,219
Show up discreetly

322
00:19:44,220 --> 00:19:45,950
and create a chance encounter.

323
00:19:46,570 --> 00:19:47,570
But he simply went to EAW

324
00:19:48,180 --> 00:19:49,219
to help out temporarily.

325
00:19:49,220 --> 00:19:50,809
I am guessing he won't stay that long.

326
00:19:50,810 --> 00:19:52,530
Anyway, let me tell you.

327
00:19:52,630 --> 00:19:54,900
You have to fight for your own happiness.

328
00:19:59,010 --> 00:19:59,640
Today,

329
00:19:59,641 --> 00:20:01,269
I really wanted to accompany you.

330
00:20:01,270 --> 00:20:03,219
But I've already promised Xia.

331
00:20:03,220 --> 00:20:04,239
Her homestay is opening,

332
00:20:04,240 --> 00:20:05,309
and I have to go help.

333
00:20:05,310 --> 00:20:05,980
It's fine.

334
00:20:05,981 --> 00:20:07,509
I have to go back and edit a video anyway.

335
00:20:07,510 --> 00:20:08,510
It's okay.

336
00:20:08,940 --> 00:20:09,610
When you're less busy,

337
00:20:09,611 --> 00:20:11,029
let's stay at the homestay together.

338
00:20:11,030 --> 00:20:12,309
Xia is really nice.

339
00:20:12,310 --> 00:20:14,570
You two will definitely be good friends.

340
00:20:16,370 --> 00:20:17,000
Okay.

341
00:20:17,001 --> 00:20:18,069
Hurry up and go do your thing.

342
00:20:18,070 --> 00:20:19,070
You...

343
00:20:21,010 --> 00:20:21,460
Okay.

344
00:20:21,461 --> 00:20:22,860
Go keep your Xia company.

345
00:20:23,330 --> 00:20:25,130
Tell me if there's any progress.

346
00:20:27,070 --> 00:20:28,070
Got it.

347
00:20:29,770 --> 00:20:30,939
You can't live on air.

348
00:20:30,940 --> 00:20:33,069
Remember to eat no matter how busy you are.

349
00:20:33,070 --> 00:20:34,070
I know.

350
00:20:34,110 --> 00:20:35,420
Bye.

351
00:20:37,810 --> 00:20:39,070
Be careful not to fall.

352
00:20:39,830 --> 00:20:40,570
If you still don't leave,

353
00:20:40,571 --> 00:20:41,739
you'll have to help me edit the video.

354
00:20:41,740 --> 00:20:42,740
Bye.

355
00:20:58,680 --> 00:20:59,680
I'm done editing!

356
00:21:05,140 --> 00:21:07,030
There's just one thing left to do.

357
00:21:16,830 --> 00:21:18,160
I'll go with this store.

358
00:21:22,590 --> 00:21:23,640
No delivery?

359
00:21:24,180 --> 00:21:26,030
How far is it from here?

360
00:21:27,680 --> 00:21:28,890
3km?

361
00:21:33,030 --> 00:21:34,360
The cab is so expensive!

362
00:21:35,300 --> 00:21:37,630
I could have a few more servings with that.

363
00:21:37,940 --> 00:21:38,940
Never mind.

364
00:21:43,290 --> 00:21:44,070
I'll just walk there.

365
00:21:44,071 --> 00:21:45,330
Consider it a workout.

366
00:21:50,500 --> 00:21:52,400
Something doesn't feel right.

367
00:21:55,070 --> 00:21:56,879
I want to drink some more!

368
00:21:56,880 --> 00:21:58,010
I'm not drunk!

369
00:21:58,380 --> 00:21:59,420
Stop drinking!
Go home now.

370
00:21:59,740 --> 00:22:01,300
No, I don't want!
I still want to drink!

371
00:22:01,330 --> 00:22:02,110
Look how much you've had.

372
00:22:02,111 --> 00:22:03,460
I'm not drunk!

373
00:22:04,830 --> 00:22:05,830
Sorry.
Hey, pretty girl.

374
00:22:05,960 --> 00:22:07,339
You almost bumped into me.

375
00:22:07,340 --> 00:22:08,879
And all you have to say is sorry?

376
00:22:08,880 --> 00:22:10,140
Where are you heading?

377
00:22:12,700 --> 00:22:14,100
Why are you running away?

378
00:22:16,700 --> 00:22:17,879
Dafeng, Dafeng.

379
00:22:17,880 --> 00:22:19,590
Don't scare the pretty girl.

380
00:22:19,730 --> 00:22:20,840
I'm just saying hi.

381
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:23,000
Pretty girl.

382
00:22:24,090 --> 00:22:25,200
Did I scare you?

383
00:22:25,440 --> 00:22:26,829
Wanna grab supper with me?

384
00:22:26,830 --> 00:22:27,830
My treat.

385
00:22:28,090 --> 00:22:29,350
Come with me, will you?

386
00:22:29,460 --> 00:22:31,320
My boyfriend is here to pick me up.

387
00:22:32,810 --> 00:22:34,509
You have no game at all.

388
00:22:34,510 --> 00:22:35,510
Fu Shizhe.

389
00:22:42,050 --> 00:22:43,180
What a coincidence.

390
00:22:43,700 --> 00:22:44,700
Shize.

391
00:22:44,830 --> 00:22:45,830
Is this your...

392
00:22:46,000 --> 00:22:47,060
What are you doing?

393
00:22:47,130 --> 00:22:49,350
I just wanted to treat her to supper.

394
00:22:51,530 --> 00:22:52,530
Do you want to go?

395
00:22:55,530 --> 00:22:56,590
You've scared her.

396
00:22:56,850 --> 00:22:57,850
Apologize.

397
00:22:59,160 --> 00:23:00,160
Okay.
I will.

398
00:23:01,140 --> 00:23:02,160
My bad.

399
00:23:05,850 --> 00:23:06,850
Say it again.

400
00:23:10,850 --> 00:23:11,850
My bad.

401
00:23:13,590 --> 00:23:14,240
Apologize properly.

402
00:23:14,241 --> 00:23:15,500
What are you sorry for?

403
00:23:16,140 --> 00:23:17,140
Dafeng.

404
00:23:23,050 --> 00:23:24,050
I'm sorry!

405
00:23:27,210 --> 00:23:28,210
Shize,

406
00:23:28,750 --> 00:23:30,350
Dafeng had too much to drink.

407
00:23:30,500 --> 00:23:31,740
Uh, sister-in-law, we're sorry.

408
00:23:32,090 --> 00:23:33,350
Don't take it to heart.

409
00:23:34,240 --> 00:23:35,200
I'll... I'll take him

410
00:23:35,201 --> 00:23:36,249
to sober up immediately.

411
00:23:36,250 --> 00:23:37,330
Let's go.

412
00:23:39,380 --> 00:23:40,380
He's drunk.

413
00:23:49,350 --> 00:23:50,350
Thank you.

414
00:23:52,240 --> 00:23:53,640
What did you just call me?

415
00:23:59,310 --> 00:24:00,500
Fu Shizhe. Fu...

416
00:24:02,250 --> 00:24:03,250
Fu Shize.

417
00:24:06,270 --> 00:24:07,720
Fu Shizhe.

418
00:24:09,900 --> 00:24:11,049
Straighten your tongue.

419
00:24:11,050 --> 00:24:12,050
Say it again.

420
00:24:14,410 --> 00:24:16,610
Fu Shize.

421
00:24:18,750 --> 00:24:19,750
Sorry.
I-I didn't mean to

422
00:24:20,400 --> 00:24:21,750
get your name wrong.

423
00:24:22,400 --> 00:24:23,850
Whenever I'm nervous, I

424
00:24:24,160 --> 00:24:25,829
can't pronounce things properly.

425
00:24:25,830 --> 00:24:27,090
How do you know my name?

426
00:24:28,330 --> 00:24:30,590
Someone at EAW said it.

427
00:24:36,200 --> 00:24:37,530
What are you doing here?

428
00:24:37,700 --> 00:24:38,700
I...

429
00:24:39,750 --> 00:24:41,550
I came to buy fried rice noodles.

430
00:24:44,140 --> 00:24:46,570
But I think I'm lost.

431
00:24:49,700 --> 00:24:51,360
The app says it's around here,

432
00:24:51,500 --> 00:24:52,500
but I don't see it.

433
00:24:54,700 --> 00:24:55,700
Let's go.

434
00:25:00,830 --> 00:25:03,030
I'll take you to get fried rice noodles.

435
00:25:19,400 --> 00:25:20,940
Can I add you on...

436
00:25:25,720 --> 00:25:27,780
Let me treat you to some rice noodles.

437
00:25:30,810 --> 00:25:31,810
No, thanks.

438
00:25:33,980 --> 00:25:35,109
Then, can I add you on...

439
00:25:35,110 --> 00:25:36,710
Miss, what do you want to add?

440
00:25:37,570 --> 00:25:38,610
We have eggs and sausages.

441
00:25:39,110 --> 00:25:40,310
You can add anything.

442
00:25:43,570 --> 00:25:44,570
Nothing, thanks.

443
00:25:53,720 --> 00:25:55,450
I hope those two people earlier

444
00:25:55,880 --> 00:25:56,940
didn't bother you.

445
00:25:59,380 --> 00:26:00,380
It's fine.

446
00:26:02,770 --> 00:26:03,770
Go home early.

447
00:26:06,200 --> 00:26:07,200
Okay.

448
00:26:09,250 --> 00:26:10,250
Fu Shize, I...

449
00:26:12,030 --> 00:26:14,130
Can I ask you a question?

450
00:26:17,460 --> 00:26:18,460
Go ahead.

451
00:26:21,310 --> 00:26:22,809
How does VR

452
00:26:22,810 --> 00:26:24,940
create such an immersive experience?

453
00:26:25,680 --> 00:26:27,110
The screen is so close,

454
00:26:27,640 --> 00:26:29,270
yet it feels so real.

455
00:26:38,270 --> 00:26:39,400
Close your left eye.

456
00:26:42,270 --> 00:26:43,870
Now switch to your right eye.

457
00:26:47,140 --> 00:26:48,219
Is there a difference?

458
00:26:48,220 --> 00:26:50,880
P-Perceptual difference?

459
00:26:52,980 --> 00:26:55,009
So, the sense of distance in VR

460
00:26:55,010 --> 00:26:57,470
is actually a carefully designed illusion.

461
00:26:58,070 --> 00:26:59,070
You can say that.

462
00:27:00,140 --> 00:27:01,670
Although it's an illusion,

463
00:27:02,110 --> 00:27:02,880
your brain will think

464
00:27:02,881 --> 00:27:04,210
it's a real experience.

465
00:27:07,110 --> 00:27:08,110
Fu Shize.

466
00:27:09,350 --> 00:27:10,350
Thank you.

467
00:27:12,830 --> 00:27:13,830
Is that all?

468
00:27:18,740 --> 00:27:19,939
C-Can I

469
00:27:19,940 --> 00:27:21,570
get your contact info?

470
00:27:25,310 --> 00:27:27,270
I-I know you have a cold.

471
00:27:27,880 --> 00:27:30,169
I heard there's a very effective medicine,

472
00:27:30,170 --> 00:27:31,970
and I want to recommend it to you.

473
00:27:34,310 --> 00:27:35,310
No, thanks.

474
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:36,510
Never mind then.

475
00:27:36,511 --> 00:27:38,240
I-I wish you a speedy recovery.

476
00:28:04,330 --> 00:28:06,770
Yun Li, what are you doing?

477
00:28:09,680 --> 00:28:12,750
So embarrassing.

478
00:28:16,480 --> 00:28:17,350
Memory erased.

479
00:28:17,351 --> 00:28:18,980
Nothing happened just now.

480
00:28:19,070 --> 00:28:20,220
Nothing happened.

481
00:28:26,920 --> 00:28:27,770
Let's ask Tang Lin.

482
00:28:27,771 --> 00:28:28,980
She might know.

483
00:28:30,050 --> 00:28:30,660
No.

484
00:28:31,070 --> 00:28:32,070
If I tell Tang Lin,

485
00:28:32,071 --> 00:28:33,420
won't everyone know?

486
00:28:34,320 --> 00:28:36,530
I'll... I'll ask Yun Ye.

487
00:28:37,180 --> 00:28:38,700
Definitely not Yun Ye.
He's just a kid.

488
00:28:38,980 --> 00:28:39,980
What does he know?

489
00:28:42,400 --> 00:28:43,460
Ask my fans.

490
00:28:46,480 --> 00:28:49,660
The fewer people know
about this, the better.

491
00:28:50,940 --> 00:28:52,100
I'll ask Baidu.

492
00:28:53,680 --> 00:28:55,800
[Being rejected when asking
someone for their WeChat]

493
00:28:58,270 --> 00:28:59,010
Was it because

494
00:28:59,011 --> 00:29:00,719
my way of asking for his WeChat was wrong,

495
00:29:00,720 --> 00:29:02,450
and I didn't make myself clear?

496
00:29:02,750 --> 00:29:05,480
I did make myself clear, didn't I?

497
00:29:06,610 --> 00:29:07,380
No.

498
00:29:07,381 --> 00:29:08,980
This answer is unreliable.

499
00:29:10,160 --> 00:29:11,420
He's just pretending.

500
00:29:11,570 --> 00:29:12,700
Playing hard to get.

501
00:29:12,960 --> 00:29:15,660
Ask a few more times
and he'll give it to you.

502
00:29:16,350 --> 00:29:17,480
Playing hard to get?

503
00:29:20,050 --> 00:29:21,650
He's not that kind of person.

504
00:29:22,850 --> 00:29:24,349
Isn't it obvious?

505
00:29:24,350 --> 00:29:25,510
It means he's

506
00:29:25,770 --> 00:29:28,070
not interested in you at all.

507
00:29:29,380 --> 00:29:32,050
That's possible.

508
00:29:34,810 --> 00:29:36,410
I didn't even get his WeChat.

509
00:29:37,510 --> 00:29:38,769
I don't know when

510
00:29:38,770 --> 00:29:41,090
I'll see him again.

511
00:29:44,350 --> 00:29:45,510
It's fine.

512
00:29:45,610 --> 00:29:47,380
We still have the noodles.

513
00:29:54,920 --> 00:29:55,920
It's cold.

514
00:29:56,070 --> 00:29:57,220
It's stone cold.

515
00:29:57,920 --> 00:29:59,850
My heart is even colder than yours.

516
00:30:11,250 --> 00:30:13,459
The missing person has finally returned!

517
00:30:13,460 --> 00:30:14,636
Grandpa,
the content creator you follow

518
00:30:14,660 --> 00:30:15,640
is finally online!

519
00:30:15,641 --> 00:30:16,849
Update already! Update already!

520
00:30:16,850 --> 00:30:18,219
Where is the promised benefit

521
00:30:18,220 --> 00:30:18,940
when you hit a million fans?

522
00:30:18,941 --> 00:30:19,979
When are you updating next?

523
00:30:19,980 --> 00:30:21,199
I'm new here. I'll come
every time from now on.

524
00:30:21,200 --> 00:30:22,140
Start a livestream quickly. I can't wait!

525
00:30:22,141 --> 00:30:23,459
When will you chat with us?

526
00:30:23,460 --> 00:30:24,609
First time here, please take care of me.

527
00:30:24,610 --> 00:30:25,849
Hello, everyone.

528
00:30:25,850 --> 00:30:28,070
I'm Idle Cloud Tick-Tock.

529
00:30:28,510 --> 00:30:29,899
Idle Cloud is finally online!

530
00:30:29,900 --> 00:30:31,139
I missed you so much.

531
00:30:31,140 --> 00:30:32,699
This is the benefit I promised all of you

532
00:30:32,700 --> 00:30:34,300
when we reach a million fans.

533
00:30:35,200 --> 00:30:36,880
Why did I change my avatar?

534
00:30:40,050 --> 00:30:42,310
Because I'm feeling a bit "zhi bi" today.

535
00:30:42,830 --> 00:30:43,820
It's "zi bi",

536
00:30:43,840 --> 00:30:45,110
not "zhi bi".

537
00:30:48,820 --> 00:30:49,959
Straighten your tongue

538
00:30:49,960 --> 00:30:50,960
and say it again.

539
00:30:52,090 --> 00:30:53,290
"Zi bi" (withdrawn).

540
00:30:53,750 --> 00:30:55,880
I didn't say it wrong this time, right?

541
00:30:56,050 --> 00:30:57,490
Idle Cloud,
how about playing a game?

542
00:30:57,660 --> 00:30:59,589
It's boring to just talk like this.

543
00:30:59,590 --> 00:31:00,740
That's true.

544
00:31:01,240 --> 00:31:03,350
So what should I play?

545
00:31:03,380 --> 00:31:04,910
How about tongue twisters?

546
00:31:05,510 --> 00:31:06,789
Okay, tongue twisters it is.

547
00:31:06,790 --> 00:31:09,450
You guys give me the
twisters and I'll read them.

548
00:31:12,250 --> 00:31:13,419
Isn't this Ms. Idle Cloud?

549
00:31:13,420 --> 00:31:15,930
Grandma Liu looks for Grandma Niu

550
00:31:15,960 --> 00:31:18,790
to buy durian milk.

551
00:31:19,610 --> 00:31:20,610
Next.

552
00:31:20,960 --> 00:31:22,289
4 is 4,

553
00:31:22,290 --> 00:31:23,610
10 is 10.

554
00:31:23,850 --> 00:31:26,160
40 is a fact,

555
00:31:26,200 --> 00:31:27,200
and a fact is...

556
00:31:30,430 --> 00:31:32,680
Why are you all laughing?

557
00:31:33,350 --> 00:31:35,549
I don't distinguish between
flat and retroflex consonants?

558
00:31:35,550 --> 00:31:36,680
It's okay, isn't it?

559
00:31:37,420 --> 00:31:38,950
Did I read it wrong just now?

560
00:31:39,960 --> 00:31:41,720
I didn't expect Ms. Idle Cloud

561
00:31:42,310 --> 00:31:43,549
to be quite introverted in private,

562
00:31:43,550 --> 00:31:45,549
yet rather extroverted when streaming.

563
00:31:45,550 --> 00:31:46,550
Ms. Idle Cloud,

564
00:31:46,730 --> 00:31:48,490
make a sentence with "shize".

565
00:31:48,520 --> 00:31:50,390
In... in fact...

566
00:31:51,750 --> 00:31:53,479
In... in fact...

567
00:31:53,480 --> 00:31:55,310
It might look like a wolf,

568
00:31:55,750 --> 00:31:57,550
but in fact, it is actually a dog.

569
00:31:59,610 --> 00:32:00,740
She's scolding you.

570
00:32:01,070 --> 00:32:02,350
She said you're a dog.

571
00:32:05,810 --> 00:32:06,810
Boring.

572
00:32:08,200 --> 00:32:09,219
This Ms. Idle Cloud is too funny.

573
00:32:09,220 --> 00:32:10,679
There's no other meaning to what I said.

574
00:32:10,680 --> 00:32:12,179
I'm just making a sentence.

575
00:32:12,180 --> 00:32:12,750
Alright.

576
00:32:12,751 --> 00:32:14,310
That's it for me today.

577
00:32:15,770 --> 00:32:17,570
I'm saying goodbye to everyone.

578
00:32:18,360 --> 00:32:19,360
She's off.

579
